  -abnormal-th float
    	path abnormality threshold (default 0.2)
  -baseline value
    	per-distance idle baseline (repeatable). KEY=BW[,LAT] e.g. local_mem=270Gbps,1400ns. Keys: same_switch, multi_switch, cross_root, cross_socket, local_mem, remote_mem. Units: bps/Gbps, ns/us. Path status is bandwidth-only; a LAT you set judges that distance's advisory idle latency_status (unset: same-distance siblings; the Fig.4 latencies are never used for it); same_switch latency also gates ACS/ATS. Unset distances keep Fig.4×line-rate defaults.
  -baseline-file string
    	JSON object of idle baselines (same keys as --baseline). Fields: bandwidth_bps or bandwidth (e.g. 270Gbps), latency_ns or latency (e.g. 1400ns). An optional "tables" object holds per-Fig.4-table sections (key line_rate=<N>Gbps[,pcie_hop=<N>Gbps]) that replace the top level for RNICs on that table. Unknown fields are rejected. Flags override the file, sections included.
  -busy-cooldown duration
    	minimum interval between PFC/drop-triggered busy runs (0 disables) (default 30s)
  -busy-interval duration
    	periodic busy-mode run on a loaded host without PFC/drops, at most once per interval (0 disables; beyond NSDI'23 §4.2)
  -busy-samples value
    	loopback readings per path on a loaded RNIC in busy mode; the median is classified, so a single noisy sample no longer marks a healthy sibling abnormal (1 disables the repeat) (default 3)
  -cpu-busy-high value
    	CPU busy fraction of a NUMA node (/proc/stat, over the poll interval) at or above which a path through its CPU package that reads abnormal is reported uncertain (cpu_busy) instead (0 disables, at most 1) (default 0.5)
  -exclude-rnic value
    	RDMA device to leave out of discovery, by IB device name (mlx5_3) or PCI address (0000:3c:00.1), repeatable or comma-separated: never probed, paired or exported (e.g. a fabric-management HCA). A name that matches no device fails start-up
  -fault string
    	simulator fault (e.g. rnic_pcie:rnic0, gpu_pcie:gpu0, upi, mesh:0-1, acs, ats, mem_flap:mem0, connect_fail:rnic0, flap:rnic0, tor, isolate:rnic3, compute_mode:gpu3, fast_rp:rp.0,rp.1)
  -flap-window int
    	consecutive gray tests on a link that diagnose flapping (default 3)
  -gpu-util-interval duration
    	minimum period between nvidia-smi GPU utilization queries (default 10s)
  -idle-gate-command string
    	daemon: executable run (no shell, no arguments) right before each idle-trigger run; exit 0 lets the run start; exit 1 (denied), exit 2 or higher (the gate could not decide), a timeout or an exec failure skips it until the next --idle-interval (e.g. a script that exits 1 while a scheduler job holds the host and 2 when the scheduler cannot be queried; empty: no gate)
  -idle-gate-timeout value
    	daemon: kill --idle-gate-command and skip the idle run when it has not exited after this long (at most 20s) (default 5s)
  -idle-interval duration
    	idle-host full-mesh interval (default 5m0s)
  -iters value
    	loopback probe iterations (small/large WRITE pairs) per measurement, 1 to 512 (default 512)
  -large-msg value
    	large-message size in bytes (bandwidth probe), at most 16 MiB (default 262144)
  -latency-floor value
    	least excess over the sibling median, on top of --abnormal-th, for a path's small-message latency to be judged abnormal against its siblings (sweep, recheck and locality shift); raise it where healthy paths jitter by more between runs (at most 10us; a set baseline LAT has no floor) (default 500ns)
  -mem-channel-capacity value
    	memory bandwidth of each mem.N link (all channels of one NUMA node, reads + writes), replacing the assumed constant (repeatable). BW for every link or mem.N=BW for one; units bps/Gbps (bits) or GB/s/GiB/s (bytes)
  -mem-warmup value
    	before each host-memory loopback probe, write the probe's NUMA-bound buffers from the CPU for this long so the memory subsystem is awake when measuring (0 = off, at most 1s; GPU endpoints unaffected)
  -metric-interval duration
    	RNIC counter poll interval (default 1s)
  -metrics string
    	Prometheus /metrics listen address (empty to disable; one-shot runs listen only when this flag is given) (default ":9464")
  -metrics-verb-durations
    	export hostping.verb.duration (2-3 series per RNIC→endpoint path); false drops the series from /metrics and OTLP, while reports and the gpu_slow_mr_reg diagnosis keep the timings (default true)
  -metrics-web-config string
    	Prometheus exporter-toolkit web config file enabling TLS and/or basic auth on the --metrics listener (empty: plain HTTP)
  -mutual-infiniband
    	include InfiniBand-link-layer RNICs in the mutual probe, paired by subnet prefix (off by default: separate fabrics sharing the default prefix fe80::/64 would pair and time out)
  -mutual-interval duration
    	daemon: every RNIC probes one random peer this often (opt-in, 0 = off: pairs are probed in a burst per engine run; ToN'24 recommends 100ms)
  -mutual-iters value
    	round trips per mutual probe burst (a pair that does not answer costs this many --mutual-timeout) (default 64)
  -mutual-msg value
    	mutual-probe UD SEND payload in bytes, 1 to 4096 and at most the port MTU (default 1)
  -mutual-scope value
    	RNIC pairs the mutual probe measures: rail (only RNICs sharing an IPv4 subnet or GID rail) or host (every RNIC, across rails too; only meaningful when the rails route to each other) (default rail)
  -mutual-timeout duration
    	wait for one mutual probe's reply before it counts as a timeout (ToN'24: 500ms) (default 500ms)
  -mutual-transport value
    	live mutual probe transport: rc (RC ping-pong; retransmission hides isolated loss) or ud (UD request/reply, one lost packet is one timeout; required by --mutual-interval) (default rc)
  -mutual-window duration
    	daemon: sliding window of the scheduled mutual probe's timeout ratio (ToN'24: 20s) (default 20s)
  -once
    	run the engine once and exit
  -otlp string
    	OTLP gRPC endpoint (or OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT): host:port, or http:// (plaintext) / https:// (TLS) URL
  -otlp-insecure
    	plaintext OTLP for a host:port endpoint (unset: OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_INSECURE, else plaintext for loopback and TLS with the system roots otherwise)
  -pfc-high float
    	Tx pause duration ratio that triggers busy diagnosis (default 0.03)
  -report-file string
    	append each report to this file as one JSON line (created 0640; reopened per report, so logrotate needs no signal)
  -report-format value
    	how each report is written to stdout: json (one compact object per line), pretty (indented JSON) or none (default: pretty for one-shot runs, json for the daemon)
  -sim
    	run against the in-process intra-host simulator
  -small-msg value
    	small-message size in bytes (latency probe), 1 to 16 MiB (a 0-byte WRITE measures nothing) (default 1)
  -state-dir string
    	daemon: keep the flapping streaks (--flap-window) and the idle-run cadence in DIR/state.json across a restart of the same boot and topology (created 0700 if missing; empty: kept in memory only; one-shot runs never touch it)
  -thp-low float
    	fraction of RNIC line rate below which the host counts as idle (default 0.05)
  -timeout duration
    	per-probe timeout (default 5s)
  -timeout-th float
    	mutual probe timeout ratio above which an RNIC is flagged (ToN'24 Timeout_th) (default 0.1)
  -topology string
    	built-in topology name (fig2; fig2-rails: the same host with one rail per RNIC; fig2-snc: the same host with sub-NUMA clustering, two NUMA nodes per package) (default "fig2")
  -topology-file string
    	JSON topology file
  -uncore-util
    	read memory-channel and inter-socket utilization from Intel uncore IMC and UPI PMUs via perf_event_open (Linux; needs CAP_PERFMON or perf_event_paranoid <= 0, and --mem-channel-capacity / --upi-capacity)
  -upi-bytes-per-flit value
    	bytes of data one UPI data-flit count (UNC_UPI_TxL_FLITS.ALL_DATA) carries, for a processor whose ratio hostping has not measured; measure it against a known cross-socket load (0 = the measured per-model ratio, at most 64)
  -upi-capacity value
    	capacity of each upi.A-B inter-socket link, replacing the assumed constant (repeatable). BW for every link or upi.A-B=BW for one; units as --mem-channel-capacity
  -util-high float
    	bus utilization that marks a link overloaded (default 0.9)
